//! The `font-weight` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the
//! weight (or boldness) of the font. The weights available depend on the `font-family` that is
//! currently set.
//!
//! Initial: normal. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - bold: Bold font weight. Same as `700`.
//! - bolder: One relative font weight heavier than the parent element. Note that only four font
//! weights are considered for relative weight calculation; see the [Meaning of relative
//! weights](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-weight#meaning_of_relative_weights)
//! section below.
//! - lighter: One relative font weight lighter than the parent element. Note that only four font
//! weights are considered for relative weight calculation; see the [Meaning of relative
//! weights](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-weight#meaning_of_relative_weights)
//! section below.
//! - normal: Normal font weight. Same as `400`.
//!
//! Grammar: <font-weight-absolute> | bolder | lighter
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4/#propdef-font-weight
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-weight
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

